There is a smooth Hamiltonian diffeomorphism $\phi$ of the closed connected symplectic six-manifold $Q^3$ such that $$\label{eq:counterexample}
 \#\mathop{\mathrm{Fix}}(\phi)=3<4=\mathop{\mathrm{Crit}}(Q^3)
                  =\operatorname{cuplength}(Q^3;\mathbb Q).$$ At least one fixed point of $\phi$ is degenerate.

Let $p=(0,0,1)$ and $e=(1,0,0)$ in $\mathbb R^3$. The smooth function $$\label{eq:three-point-function}
  f\colon S^2\times S^2\longrightarrow\mathbb R,
  \qquad f(x,y)=e\cdot x+(x-p)\cdot y,$$ has exactly three critical points.

After constant rescaling, the metrics in <a href="#eq:sequence" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:sequence">[eq:sequence]</a> satisfy $$\label{eq:normalization}
 \frac1V\int_M R\,d\mu=12,\qquad
 \left\lVert R-12\right\rVert_2\le4\left\lVert E\right\rVert_2,\qquad
 \left\lVert \mathop{\mathrm{Ric}}-3g\right\rVert_2\longrightarrow0,$$ where $V=\mathop{\mathrm{Vol}}(M,g)$. There are uniform positive constants $v_0,V_0,D_0$ such that $$\label{eq:initial-geometry}
 v_0\le V\le V_0,\qquad \mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(M,g)\le D_0.$$

There is a uniform $v_*>0$ such that at every time covered by Proposition <a href="#prop:tail" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:tail">7</a>, $$\label{eq:noncollapse}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Vol}}_{g_j(t)}B_{g_j(t)}(x,r)\ge v_*r^4
 \quad\text{for all }x\in M_j,\quad 0<r\le1.$$

For all sufficiently large $j$, the flow $g_j(t)$ exists on $[0,T]$. There is a uniform constant $A$ such that $$\label{eq:curvature-bound}
 \max_{M_j}|\mathop{\mathrm{Rm}}_{g_j(t)}|\le\frac At,
 \qquad 0<t<T.$$

Set $\lambda(t)=3/(1-6t)$. Along the flows above, $$\label{eq:einstein-defect}
 \sup_{0\le t<T}
 \left\lVert \mathop{\mathrm{Ric}}_{g_j(t)}-\lambda(t)g_j(t)\right\rVert_{L^2(g_j(t))}
 \longrightarrow0.$$

There is a uniform constant $C$ such that $$\label{eq:sectional-defect}
 \int_{M_j}F(\mathop{\mathrm{Rm}}_{g_j(t)})\,d\mu_{g_j(t)}\le Ct,
 \qquad 0\le t<T.$$
